  "description": "The FULL generated Microsoft.Chaos v2 Workspaces provider-operation surface at 2026-05-01-preview, drawn from the Operations_List (GetOperations) snapshot (VF9, VF12, DX1). This is deliberately the complete workspaces/scenarios/configurations/validations/runs operation tree plus the provider-level operations — not a curated subset — so a negative search over it is meaningful: it proves the only cancel operation in the scenario journey is runs/cancel/action, that there is NO validations-cancel and NO execute-cancel operation (VF9), and that Microsoft.Chaos/workspaces/scenarios/run/action does not exist (DX1). It also shows the operations the journey does NOT invoke (workspaces/read, locations/workspaceOperationResults/read) exist in the provider yet are excluded from PROVIDER_OPERATIONS (VF12). The five operations the client invokes are validate/action, validations/read, execute/action, runs/read, and runs/cancel/action.",
